  "scope": "One disposable Kubernetes v1.36.1 Kind cluster and one case-owned, single-replica Python mock endpoint. A bounded, fixed-marker streaming filter receives three benign fixture chunks and holds at most a chunk plus the longest marker window. Separate loopback HTTP clients collect the disabled-filter control and enabled-filter response over HTTP/1.1 chunked encoding, with a client acknowledgement before the source releases the rest. The evidence establishes only withholding of one fixture-designated dummy word across chunk seams while a permitted public synthetic marker remains visible. It does not validate real PII/secret classes, policy classifiers, real protocols or serving stacks, model safety, or production controls.",
